  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v4.0.0 — security-hardening release (no Critical findings across a multi-round audit). Tessera.Cryptography is now CONSTANT-TIME (limb-based secp256k1 + branchless scalar multiplication, cross-checked against an independent BouncyCastle oracle) and rejects non-canonical point/scalar encodings. Adds controller-authenticated wallet binding (BOLA fix), issuer trust-root protection, and attestation expiry caps. (breaking) Removed the legacy Tessera.Crypto / Tessera.Security duplicate crypto stack this meta-package shipped alongside Tessera.Cryptography — use Tessera.Cryptography (Pedersen / Bulletproofs / secp256k1) directly. See CHANGELOG.md and docs/security-audit-readiness.md.",
